From 4b979d8bd9bb64a0dea3ccf62494e2a04854dc0e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vic-lsh <40274755+vic-shihang-li@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 04:14:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] window: measure a fixed wall-clock window instead of a
 fixed amount of work

--warmup-secs W --duration-secs D (YAML replay.window) bound a run by time:
t0 is when measured replay starts, after the prefix-cache preflight, and the
window is [t0+W, t0+W+D). At its end admission stops, sessions release no
further rounds, tool waits are abandoned, and every in-flight request is
dropped mid-stream, closing its connection. Abandoned requests are logged
as CANCELLED_AT_WINDOW_END and are not failures; real failures still are.

Each request is stamped on the window's clock (send time, first output,
every token-id event with its own token count) and a pure fold derives:
throughput from tokens whose event arrived in the window, TTFT over
requests sent in the window with still-waiting ones censored at window end,
and TPOT as token_delivery_tpot_ms restricted to in-window events. These
replace the run-wide values in replay.common; replay.window carries W, D
and the counts. Step counts cover steps that reached a verdict inside the
window. Accepted only for saturated text replay in one process.

Without the flags nothing changes: no window block, no new status, and the
JSONL record contract is untouched.

